@anon.152f57749fcdf0a673d809c4f4545e7f.679 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [589 x i8] }> <{ [589 x i8] c"Emphasizes content by toggling italics.\0A\0A- If the current [text style]($text.style) is `{\22normal\22}`, this turns it\0A  into `{\22italic\22}`.\0A- If it is already `{\22italic\22}` or `{\22oblique\22}`, it turns it back to\0A  `{\22normal\22}`.\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0AThis is _emphasized._ \\\0AThis is #emph[too.]\0A\0A#show emph: it => {\0A  text(blue, it.body)\0A}\0A\0AThis is _emphasized_ differently.\0A```\0A\0A# Syntax\0AThis function also has dedicated syntax: To emphasize content, simply\0Aenclose it in underscores (`_`). Note that this only works at word\0Aboundaries. To emphasize part of a word, you have to use the function." }>, align 1
