@anon.152f57749fcdf0a673d809c4f4545e7f.897 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [778 x i8] }> <{ [778 x i8] c"Captured arguments to a function.\0A\0A# Argument Sinks\0ALike built-in functions, custom functions can also take a variable number of\0Aarguments. You can specify an _argument sink_ which collects all excess\0Aarguments as `..sink`. The resulting `sink` value is of the `arguments`\0Atype. It exposes methods to access the positional and named arguments.\0A\0A```example\0A#let format(title, ..authors) = {\0A  let by = authors\0A    .pos()\0A    .join(\22, \22, last: \22 and \22)\0A\0A  [*#title* \\ _Written by #by;_]\0A}\0A\0A#format(\22ArtosFlow\22, \22Jane\22, \22Joe\22)\0A```\0A\0A# Spreading\0AInversely to an argument sink, you can _spread_ arguments, arrays and\0Adictionaries into a function call with the `..spread` operator:\0A\0A```example\0A#let array = (2, 3, 5)\0A#calc.min(..array)\0A#let dict = (fill: blue)\0A#text(..dict)[Hello]\0A```" }>, align 1
